  "review_facts": [
    "The nine changed Python sources were reviewed as a unit. They implement attraction-count constraints and reported conflicts, entrance metadata, and deterministic request fingerprints. They add no native loading, process launch, database import, filesystem pattern, or binary journal path.",
    "The installed ELF import audit found no libc regex or glob imports in the Python runtime and extensions. The remaining command-line, package manager and PAM callers remain outside the Uvicorn service entry point. The Python application uses a fixed pathlib pattern on the configured knowledge directory.",
    "No inspected ELF imports wide scanf. The application has no user-supplied native format strings, executable inputs, ldd entry point, or extension installation route.",
    "The libsystemd and libudev binaries and package revisions match the prior assessment. lslogins is the only observed dynamic journal reader. Its process and binary journal files are outside the execution flow.",
    "SQLite package and shared library bytes match the prior assessment. Database paths still come from service configuration and fixed filenames. Uploads and SQL parameters do not supply a database file or raw SQL.",
    "The finding identities and prior exact predicates are carried forward. No additional advisories are classified by this review. All raw Grype results remain available and the release gate still checks every severity."
  ]
}
